  "scope": "C++/Python synchronous RGB entire-stack preparation matches 5292 actual ImageJ 1.54r private applyRGBStack reference rows: seven endpoint pairs, seven component masks, nine selection forms, three C/Z/T anchors, optional promoted stages and whole-active-plane policy. The actual macro-confirmed GenericDialog and post-commit setup execute with only plot/label/scrollbar presentation bypasses; processing sources and bytecode are unmodified. The oracle was corrected to use actual setup/getProcessor/snapshot promotion boundaries after its initial point-selection mismatch; failed logs and variants remain. A final test-only amendment replaces an invalid no-op preview-wrapper identity assertion with a committed owner/history identity assertion; compiled native/SDK bytes are unchanged and both installed suites rerun against the final test snapshot. The active preview maps once through promoted stages; other TCZ planes use only the current component and Java-int-narrowed processor bounds. Non-area processor ROI/mask asymmetry, fractional/degenerate/extreme endpoints, source geometry, private preparation, one paired Undo/Redo, stale-domain refusal, freeze-before-callback, cancellation/failure, admission, unsupported storage and empty membership/progress are tested. Source metadata is admitted before resolving target copies. Limits conservatively cover owned mapping/output/mask/geometry/transaction work; caller/source/provider caches, history/publication staging and total RSS are external. Windows/Linux each pass 22 native suites, three existing C++ workflow/batch/RGB UI regression probes, installed SDK consumer, ten background repetitions, four hidden GL contexts and 20577 installed Python checks (5315 new), zero failure/error/skip. Each installed test uses its actual disposable venv interpreter; source/module origins and 5475 native Linux test/config/fixture files are pinned. Exact owned scratch is archived and every member CRC/SHA verified before confined removal; final installed prefixes and native/SDK probes remain. This service is not yet integrated into captured stack commands, leased jobs, portable replay or actual ImGui stack controls. Existing command wire contracts, registration/dependency inventory and all 99 requirement/status triples remain unchanged; the old Auto producer-source gate remains open.",
